<main class="shell prose-page legal-draft"><p class="eyebrow">Draft for review</p><h1>Kredit terms</h1><aside><strong>These terms are not active yet</strong><p>Kredit has not launched. Final terms, dates and company details must be added and approved before anyone is asked to agree.</p></aside><p class="lede">Kredit helps a seller record goods given to a customer who will pay later. The seller owns the goods, chooses the customer and decides whether to allow payment later. Kredit is not the lender.</p><section><h2>The final terms will explain</h2><ul><li>Who can use Kredit and who can act for a business.</li><li>When a sale becomes agreed and when goods are handed over.</li><li>How payments, bank debit, fees, refunds and failed payments work.</li><li>How to report a problem, get help or stop using Kredit.</li><li>What happens if Kredit or a payment company is unavailable.</li><li>Which Nigerian laws apply.</li></ul></section><section><h2>How the product protects people</h2><ul><li>You see the goods, amount and payment day before you agree.</li><li>You can stop bank debit permission.</li><li>Money connected to a reported problem can be paused while it is checked.</li><li>Kredit keeps a record of what each person saw and agreed to.</li></ul></section><a class="primary-button" href="/how-it-works">See how Kredit works</a></main>
